<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela doctors to consider 65 pct offer Monday.</title>
<headline>Venezuela doctors to consider 65 pct offer Monday.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Striking Venezuelan doctors will consider a 65 percent pay offer on Monday at a general meeting of the Venezuelan Physicians Association (FMV), sources at the Health Ministry said.</p>
<p>The offer tops previous government proposals of a 25 percent rise, but still falls short of the 300 percent increase doctors - -- who began striking Dec 28 -- had been holding out for.</p>
<p>FMV officials are due to meet with the Labor Ministry Friday afternoon to discuss the proposal.</p>
<p>A truce that has maintained staffing at emergency wards during the strike will remain in place until the FMV's Monday general meeting. It was originally set to expire last Wednesday night.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
